00:05:21.817 --> 00:05:23.002
It's so important.

00:05:23.002 --> 00:05:24.523
It's inspiring,

00:05:24.523 --> 00:05:26.593
And it it's just an incredible thing,

00:05:26.593 --> 00:05:28.139
And everybody else, maybe hasn't seen it.

00:05:28.139 --> 00:05:29.859
So maybe tell them
what, what was the idea?

00:05:29.859 --> 00:05:31.075
Why did y'all start this?

00:05:31.075 --> 00:05:33.729
- Well, so we had written
The Book of Gutsy Women

00:05:33.729 --> 00:05:36.545
a few years ago, which
really was the continuation

00:05:36.545 --> 00:05:38.810
of a conversation we've
been having my whole life

00:05:38.810 --> 00:05:42.310
about inspiring a dynamic and gutsy women.

00:05:43.275 --> 00:05:46.243
Some in my life, my grandmothers
were both incredibly

00:05:46.243 --> 00:05:47.161
gutsy women.

00:05:47.161 --> 00:05:47.994
- Yeah.

00:05:47.994 --> 00:05:51.331
- To women that my mother
kind of brought into my life,

00:05:51.331 --> 00:05:54.258
to women whose stories
she would share with me,

00:05:54.258 --> 00:05:58.339
her being inspired by Helen
Keller and Harriet Tubman,

00:05:58.339 --> 00:06:01.882
and then as I got older Kelly,
I got to return that favor

00:06:01.882 --> 00:06:04.961
bringing inspiring gutsy women who I knew,

00:06:04.961 --> 00:06:06.467
kind of to my mom's attention.

00:06:06.467 --> 00:06:08.449
So we wrote this book, and then
we had the chance to turn it

00:06:08.449 --> 00:06:13.155
in to a series with Apple TV
Plus and understandably, Kelly,

00:06:13.155 --> 00:06:15.858
like they were like, you
have so many amazing women,

00:06:15.858 --> 00:06:18.467
many of them are not with us any longer,

00:06:18.467 --> 00:06:22.800
so we have to kind of expand
kind of the, the window

00:06:23.715 --> 00:06:27.075
of who we're looking at, so
that we can actually, you know,

00:06:27.075 --> 00:06:29.217
talk to the women that
we're gonna feature,

00:06:29.217 --> 00:06:31.459
and have shared experiences,
whether, you know, painting-

00:06:31.459 --> 00:06:32.785
- [Kelly] That's helpful.

00:06:32.785 --> 00:06:35.448
- with Megan Thee
Stallion or going kayaking

00:06:35.448 --> 00:06:38.051
and canoeing with a
former white supremacist

00:06:38.051 --> 00:06:38.953
which was one of the more-

00:06:38.953 --> 00:06:40.280
- [Kelly] that was such
an intriguing episode.

00:06:40.280 --> 00:06:41.961
- extraordinary moments we had,

00:06:41.961 --> 00:06:44.122
to going to a comedy show to listen

00:06:44.122 --> 00:06:47.416
to these amazing gutsy women,
you know, tell jokes on stage.

00:06:47.416 --> 00:06:49.241
And so it just, it really it,

00:06:49.241 --> 00:06:51.139
it at times was a literal road trip,

00:06:51.139 --> 00:06:52.858
at times it was a more metaphorical one.

00:06:52.858 --> 00:06:57.608
Hello COVID, and yet it was
such a joy and a privilege to

00:06:58.787 --> 00:07:00.649
be able to learn these
gutsy women stories,

00:07:00.649 --> 00:07:02.435
share these gutsy women stories,

00:07:02.435 --> 00:07:03.482
and spend time with my mom.

00:07:03.482 --> 00:07:04.858
(Hilary laughs)

00:07:04.858 --> 00:07:05.691
(audience claps)

00:07:05.691 --> 00:07:06.524
- Absolutely.

00:07:06.524 --> 00:07:07.357
Well, and I, I want,

00:07:07.357 --> 00:07:08.698
I'm so glad that's like
the greatest segue,

00:07:08.698 --> 00:07:10.520
because watching y'all, it felt

00:07:10.520 --> 00:07:12.593
that's what I think
people are gonna love too.

00:07:12.593 --> 00:07:14.334
It is very cool how y'all talk about

00:07:14.334 --> 00:07:16.056
that you don't always agree

00:07:16.056 --> 00:07:16.889
on everything.

00:07:16.889 --> 00:07:17.722
- [Hilary] Right.

00:07:17.722 --> 00:07:18.648
- And that you learn
from each other that way,

00:07:18.648 --> 00:07:20.227
because I think it's very important.

00:07:20.227 --> 00:07:24.049
My mother and I, you know,
on some pretty big topics,

00:07:24.049 --> 00:07:25.690
